 In the odd-numbered year 2007, (2007 is not divisible by 31, consider the next odd-numbered year 2009) 2009 is not divisible by 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, and so on. So we only need to consider numbers up to 31, since the larger odd numbers sharing common factors with 2009 are multiples of odd numbers up to 31. 2009 ÷ 5 = 401.8, 2009 ÷ 7 = 287, 2009 ÷ 11 = 182.6, 2009 ÷ 13 = 154.53, 2009 ÷ 17 = 118.17, 2009 ÷ 19 = 105.74, 2009 ÷ 23 = 87.35, 2009 ÷ 29 = 69.28, 2009 ÷ 31 = 64.805, and 5 does not divide evenly into 2009. Therefore, the largest number that can cleanly divide 2009 from the list of choices is 7. However, in 2009, there is no lucky number between 1 and 7 that will work so whatever number we manually test from 1 - 7  is 7.  Any other odd number up to 2009 is divisible by 7 (e.g., 2013 = 301 x 7 or 2017 = 288 x 7, etc.  
Therefore, it is a sufficient test to manually check for years');
answer>2015</answer>

